# Ownership seams, made reviewable.
#
# GitHub reads this file from .github/ at the repo root; each line pairs a path
# with the owners whose review a change needs (it bites once branch
# protection's "Require review from Code Owners" is switched on).
#
# The seam that matters in a SpecAssay-governed repo is the registry — the
# intent side of the thread. Dev, or an agent, may DRAFT a restatement; the
# owner APPROVES it. The Thread Report's Intent Changed section is the
# tripwire (no restatement lands silently); this file is the lock (no
# restatement merges without a named human). See
# docs/scope-and-pull-requests.md §5a.
#
# In your own repo the line reads e.g.:
#   PRD.md  @your-org/product

# The example app's registry (its PRD) answers to the product owner.
/examples/example-app/PRD.md @rdryfoos
